notes: 'Imported from CultureBotHT (consolidated_media.json (media-only)). Used in
  61 CultureBot media; samples: ShewMM, YCFA, MG minimal media…. No CAS-RN or CHEBI
  mapping available; reviewed on 2026-05-11 as a named vitamin stock/pre-mix pending
  component-level recipe curation.


  Source-continuity correction proposal under issue1237 TV-003: Current CultureBotHT
  generic source definition, distinct from its ATCC/MD-VS block. The exact Mixes.csv
  block names ten solutes at the printed mg/L values and labels the preparation X=100
  / Standard 100X vitamin solution. Values are transcribed without multiplying or
  dividing by X, and receiving doses are unchanged. Carrier, solvent quantity, preparation
  process and purchase/lot identity are not specified in this block. Cyanocobalamin
  is explicit here; no exact cyanocobalamin identity is transferred to JCM197/NBRC837/NBRC903
  generic Vitamin B12. The preserved W09 precursor deliberately left all ten references
  UNMAPPED pending child review. The current W08 successor binds nine explicit named
  inputs to matching current MIM catalog entities after source/form review. Calcium
  pantothenate alone remains UNMAPPED because the source gives no D/DL designation
  while active CHEBI:31345 is D-specific. Lipoic acid is generic, not an R/S or racemate
  assertion; explicit CB cyanocobalamin is not transferred to generic JCM/NBRC Vitamin
  B12. These component assertions do not approve inherited child aliases, properties,
  roles or whole-stock equivalence.


  Separate genuine NCMA source claim, preserved rather than refuted: NCMA Medium6
  Wolfe''s Vitamin Solution explicitly prints composition per liter: pyridoxine HCl10mg;
  thiamine HCl5mg; riboflavin5mg; nicotinic acid5mg; calcium pantothenate5mg; p-aminobenzoic
  acid5mg; thioctic acid5mg; biotin2mg; folic acid2mg; Vitamin B12 0.1mg; potassium
  phosphate monobasic900mg. It directs addition to distilled water and filter sterilization,
  without a literal 1.0L/L water quantity. Source https://ncma.bigelow.org/PDF%20Files/NCMA%20Medium%206%20Wolfe%27s%20Vitamin%20Solution.pdf
  ; exact current PDF SHA256 b7bbf28efb43cfee8476e83780a55d929e574f3f0b7479583926d927409b4615,
  accessed2026-11-08T08:27:46.568100+00:00. This positive phosphate-containing source
  definition is not established as the CultureBotHT generic formulation. The September2026
  NCMA annotation and all original component/role assertions remain preserved in the
  authentic beforeimage and unchanged history; the source itself is not wrong. No
  NCMA owner is minted or merged here.


  The original occurrence_statistics61 is retained as the historical imported count;
  later available source versions enumerate62 and63 and do not prove April membership.
  All original source histories, aliases and identifiers remain. Legacy NCMA-based
  nutritional role evidence is retained without renewed role or source-equivalence
  approval. The nominal JCM197/NBRC837/NBRC903 report is supported separately; its
  eventual common owner scope is not selected by this correction, and its unknown
  B12 form is neither equated to nor declared different from the explicit CultureBotHT
  cyanocobalamin input. All8cases71CMoccurrences84KGholds and6exclusions remain outside
  automatic mapping release.


  Issue1237 current comparator supersession: this existing CultureBotHT owner correction
  is causally required by the NBRC903 comparison in W08 case CM_NAME:d57e91ffaea6f0ab6ff0f3d6f0b04c26356c832e85dd83e9e2319874fda43506,
  triggered only by CM_OCC:a181b24b7eb91c50c771bd1c1fc3012fd0cf28f45b49f2750c3d43bda9cdd531
  (CultureMech:007503, frozen NBRC_904.yaml ingredient9). None of the six NBRC case
  observations is asserted to be a CB occurrence; zero CB campaign occurrences are
  claimed. The original NBRC903 new-owner proposal and its null beforeimage remain
  immutable reconciliation input. JCM197/NBRC837/NBRC903 support one common nominal
  ten-vitamin recipe with 1L distilled-water input batch and source-specific preparation;
  generic B12 and unspecified calcium-pantothenate stereochemistry remain explicit.
  Exact association with this CB concentration/X100 definition is unproven. The W06
  JCM197 and W08 NBRC903 source-number candidates require central duplicate reconciliation,
  not installation as two owners or a new human-permission requirement. No W06 case
  ownership, nominal identifier mint, dose scaling, global exact alias, maintained
  application or role/export approval is introduced.'
